<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's Petron reduces LPG price.</title>
<headline>Manila's Petron reduces LPG price.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil refiner Petron Corp said on Friday it will cut the price of its liquefied petroleum gasoline (lpg) by five pesos per 11-kilogram cylinder to 174.30 pesos.</p>
<p>In a statement, Petron said the price adjustment will take effect on Monday. The price of 174.30 pesos is exclusive of delivery cost, the company said.</p>
<p>Petron's announcement came shortly after one of its rivals, Pilipinas Shell Petroleum Corp announced a five peso reduction in its 11-kg cylinder lpg to 172 pesos effective tomorrow.</p>
<p>The country's third refiner, Caltex Philippines Inc, is yet to announce adjustments. Caltex officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 632 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
